Package: ak820-dongle-fix
Version: @VERSION@-1
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Luke <11366524+druby-luke@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: systemd, udev
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/druby-luke/ak820-dongle-linux-fix
Description: Keep the Ajazz AK820 Pro 2.4G receiver working after keyboard sleep
 The Ajazz AK820 Pro 2.4G receiver (SONiX 0c45:fdfd "2.4G Dongle") stops
 working on Linux after the keyboard has slept, because nothing reads its
 two vendor HID interfaces. This package adds a udev rule and a sandboxed
 systemd service that keep those interfaces polled, the way Windows does.
